sn1.18:1.1 starts: “Who in the world
sn1.18:1.2 starts: is a man constrained by shame,
sn1.18:1.3 starts: who awakens to censure
sn1.18:1.4 starts: like a fine stallion to the whip?”
mn143:17.15 starts: As for Sāriputta:
mn143:17.16 starts: Any monk who has gone beyond,
mn143:17.17 starts: at best can only equal him
mn143:17.18 starts: in discernment, virtue, & calm.
mn143:19.16 starts: As for Sāriputta:
mn143:19.17 starts: Any monk who has gone beyond,
mn143:19.18 starts: at best can only equal him
mn143:19.19 starts: in discernment, virtue, & calm.
sn1.17:1.1 starts: For the inexperienced,
sn1.17:1.2 starts: hard to do,
sn1.17:1.3 starts: for many are the confinements there
sn1.17:1.4 starts: in which a fool sinks.
